    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d545">

                <pb facs="0669" n="567" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg567"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Reid to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-04-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 16, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 582.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to Mr. Carter’s No. 567 of
                    the 31st ultimo, relating to the annexation of the Kongo by Belgium, which
                    inclosed a copy of a dispatch on that subject from Sir Edward Grey to the
                    British minister at Brussels, in which reference was made to a memorandum which
                    should have accompanied the dispatch, I now have <pb facs="0670" n="568"
                        xml:id="pg568"/> the honor to inclose<anchor n="1" xml:id="d545-f1"/>
                    herewith a copy of the memorandum in question, which I have received to-day from
                    the foreign office.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitelaw Reid.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d545-f1" n="1" xml:id="d545-f1-content">
                <p>See Africa No. 3, printed in S. Doc. No. 147, 61st Cong., 1st sess., entitled
                    “Affairs in the Kongo.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
